00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
so you're thinking about buying  samsung's new galaxy buds live  for your iphone but the biggest question  is how well do they work  if you don't own an android phone well  i've been using them with my iphone for  a week now so i'll give you not only the  downsides and limitations  but also a surprising benefit that i  found that you gain  if you have an iphone i think for a lot  of ios users the galaxy buds might be a  better buy than the earpods  but not for everyone let's start out  with the benefits the biggest one for me  is the sound quality not only do the  buds live sound better than the regular  airpods but they sound  even better than the pros now is it a  massive difference  no but when i put my airpod pros back  into my ears yesterday after using these  for a week  i could definitely tell the difference  and i missed the rich sound that the  lives give you  with their 12 millimeter drivers they're  also less expensive about 70 dollars  less than the pros  and 30 less than the regular ear pods  with the charging case  but both of those could be purchased a  little bit cheaper now we'll leave links  to the best deals for all three down in  the description  battery life is also better rated at  eight hours for the buds and a total of  28 hours in the case if you have active  noise cancellation disabled  which we'll definitely have to talk  about in just a bit a big benefit for me  is that they don't stick out of your  ears  i love the look it provides and they  don't snag if i'm putting on a helmet a  hat or  anything else really now if you're  somebody that hates having the mini  toothbrush or the hair dryer look  sticking out of your ears  or you just don't want to blend in with  everybody else as earpods  the buds life are great they're also  really comfortable  for me but that will depend on your ears  they don't seal  into your ear canal which helps compared  to the buds plus so they're now about as  comfortable as  earpods i was also pleasantly surprised  by how well they stay in my  ears and if regular airpods fall out for  you these most likely will not  because they do have those wing tips  that you can actually change out to get  a better seal  which of course you can't do with  standard earpods if you have other  reasons for getting them for your iphone  let me know down in the comments section  below now another thing that surprised  me was how  quickly and consistently they connected  to my iphone  the original buds were noticeably worse  than the earpods with that h1 chip  but these are super quick you do miss  out on icloud integration so you'll have  to go into the settings of each ios or  mac device  but the buds live do support multiple  saved connections and they'll  automatically disconnect from my phone  if i select them from my mac's bluetooth  menu just like the airpods  i have to say that it's very interesting  that samsung went the opposite way of  apple  and when they added active noise  cancellation they got rid of the in-ear  seal design  because of this the active noise  cancellation can only remove frequencies  lower than 700 hertz and to be honest  unless you have a constant low noise  without other medium and high frequency  sounds it's kind of pointless it will  definitely get rid of my low  ac vent sound but then my mind starts  focusing in on the higher sounds and  it's even more annoying  and when i was mowing my lawn just a few  days ago it literally  did nothing to enable the active noise  cancellation  so don't buy them for your iphone  instead of airpod pros  if you need active noise cancellation  because of this the lives  are more like the original air pods just  with a little boost  probably added for marketing now there  is a plus sign if you like to listen to  music but also be aware of your  environment these are great for that  just like the regular airpods but with  that you also get that same  big amount of sound leakage if you turn  the volume up now let's talk about  connectivity  software and a bonus for iphone users  i'm so glad that samsung has the galaxy  buds app for iphone and now they keep  updating it i set mine up using the app  and everything connected quickly but it  gave me a prompt to check the bluetooth  settings to make sure that both  bluetooth modes  are connected which they weren't this  part is important as i noticed a glitch  every once in a while  my buds live wouldn't show up in the  audio options but they did show up as  connected in the galaxy buds app i went  into the settings and only the low power  mode was connected so i had to manually  connect to the normal mode  to be able to use them one of these  times the normal mode wouldn't let me  connect  so i actually had to press and reset  them and then reconnect i did figure out  that this was only happening  if i was switching from an android  device to my iphone  and apart from that it would work  perfectly so hopefully they'll fix this  in firmware which you can thankfully  also update using the ios app  and thankfully that app matches most of  the features to android now here are the  things that you'll miss out on  the biggest bummer for me is their  notifications being read out loud  i love having siri read my text with the  earpods you're just  not gonna get that the same thing goes  with bixby on demand  if you have a samsung phone and if you  want to use bixby at all  now you could still use siri by setting  up the customizable touch options to  invoke  your assistant in those touch options  you also won't have the option for one  touch spotify  now an alternative is just setting it  for siri and then asking her to play  spotify or anything else  but that does take a little bit longer  next up is the gaming mode which lowers  latency and  almost matches airpods in ios since the  galaxy buds  also use aac there's no lag when you're  watching  videos but if you're playing a game the  sound will be about a half a second off  compared to about 150 milliseconds so if  you play a lot of games that's one area  where the buds live  won't do as good the last thing that i  missed is the ability to quickly change  bluetooth to my earpods  by pressing on the stem this is helpful  if your phone auto connects to another  bluetooth device but with the buds live  i have to pull out my phone in order to  manually switch it back  now for the one benefit of using the  lives with an  iphone they are surprisingly louder  i would say to get them to match with  the volume on my s20 ultra i have to  lower my iphone to  just over one click lower now they  aren't quiet with the samsung but i do  appreciate having the extra boost when  i'm listening to quieter youtube videos  or podcasts  overall if you don't need hands-free  siri with the text readouts or the low  latency in games i think that the galaxy  buds live  absolutely destroyed the original  earpods now it's a little bit more tough  comparing them to my pros  if you're using an iphone especially if  you want the active noise cancellation  but if you don't need that or the  hands-free siri then the lower cost  and better sounding quality is really  intriguing  and they work surprisingly well with  your iphone  i think that for many iphone users the  buds live  will work quite well and i will  definitely be using mine  a fair bit if you guys want to see my  full real world review  click up there to subscribe and if you  want to see some great galaxy buds  live videos and comparisons to the pros  you guys can check those out right over  there  this one max and i will see you in the  next one

